    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Box&nbsp;2.10</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria for <em>SMO</em>-related Curry&ndash;Jones syndrome</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Andrew O.M. Wilkie",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"775\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Essential:</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Identification of the <em>SMO</em> NM_005631.5:c.1234C&gt;T nucleotide transition in samples from more than one tissue site</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">OR</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Identification of <em>SMO</em> NM_005631.5:c.1234C&gt;T in a single tissue sample, accompanied by at least one desirable feature involving a different organ or different part of the same organ</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Desirable:</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 581.2pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"775\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">One or more of:</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">1. Swirling epidermal involvement often following Blaschko lines, with macules and/or papules, hyperpigmentation or hypopigmentation, hypertrichosis and/or atrophoderma, palmar or plantar pits</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">2. Ocular malformations (coloboma, cataract, microphthalmia)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">3. Abnormal skull (unilateral craniosynostosis, macrocephaly) or dentition</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">4. Brain malformations (partial agenesis of corpus callosum, hemimegalencephaly, polymicrogyria) that can be associated with developmental delay and intellectual disability</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">5. Medulloblastoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">6. Intestinal involvement (dysmotility, malrotation, pseudo-obstruction, hamartomas, leiomyomas, myofibromas)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1cm; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 552.85pt; background: #f0f7fc; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"737\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">7. Limb shortening, polydactyly and/or syndactyly</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
